From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Host screenshot of the presented frame
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host convenience outside the emulated hardware.

aurora_request_video_screenshot(path) asks for the next successfully presented
frame. The VI output work copies its desktop signal exactly as drawn into the
window viewport (same copy pipeline, no black bars) into a readback buffer,
submitted with that frame. After Present the buffer is mapped asynchronously
and the PNG (8-bit RGB) is encoded on its own thread, written to a temporary
file and renamed, so presentation never waits for it. A frame that is not
presented keeps the request for the next one. Apply after 0068.
